$DIR/main.p:6:1: //pu:stack: invalid size "2T" (want a number of bytes with an optional K, M or G suffix)
    //pu:stack sets the size of the stack a hosted program runs on: the runtime
    reserves that much address space before main starts. It belongs on func main
    in package main, and takes a size in bytes, with an optional K, M or G
    suffix, from 64K to 64G. A freestanding program sets up its own stack, so
    the directive has nothing to act on there.
    Put it on main:
        //pu:stack 256M
        func main() { ... }
    (see "Directives" in the Plutonium spec, section 20.3)
    (run "pluto explain E2560" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:3:1: //pu:stack applies only to func main in package main
    (explained above; run "pluto explain E2560" for more)
